prompt:
You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 4. Complete/delete commands + validation
Objective: Add complete/delete flows with good error handling and state validation.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Enhance TaskForge with a typed data model, JSON persistence, and a CLI surface that supports listing and filtering tasks (status, priority, tags, search) via a minimal Bun-based CLI skeleton.
Decisions: Use Bun for the CLI surface with a small in-repo command registry and manual argv parsing; Store tasks in a project-local JSON file at .taskforge/tasks.json with a TaskStore wrapper; Extend the in-code Task model to include priority and tags, plus a query shape for filtering; Write to a temp file and rename for safer in-place persistence; keep persistence API surface minimal for upcoming commands; Keep CLI code modular: src/cli.ts bootstrapping, src/commands/* for commands, src/storage.ts for persistence, src/task.ts for model and filters
Risks: Manual argument parsing may become brittle with complex flag combinations or edge cases; Atomic write semantics may vary across filesystems/environments; ensure temp file handling is robust; Backward compatibility: older stored tasks may lack new fields like priority/tags; runtime validation required
Snippets: export type TaskPriority = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'; | export interface Task {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  status: TaskStatus;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  description?: string;
  priority?: TaskPriority;
  tags?: string[];
} | const STORE_PATH = '.taskforge/tasks.json';
